  # --- Reverse engineering and key discovery -----------------------------------
  - type: thesis
    title: >-
      Data Reverse Engineering: from a Relational Database System to a
      3-Dimensional Conceptual Schema
    authors:
      - family-names: Bird
        given-names: L. J.
        name-suffix: (née Campbell)
    thesis-type: PhD
    institution:
      name: University of Queensland
    year: 1997
    notes: >-
      The method reverse/ follows rule by rule
      (reverse/relational-to-orm-reverse-engineering.md): the extraction
      steps, the population analysis (Step 9), the abstraction levels
      (model/abstract.py), and the DREC case study (Appendix F.2).
  - type: article
    title: Abstractions — making flat conceptual schemas more comprehensible
    authors:
      - family-names: Campbell
        given-names: L. J.
      - family-names: Halpin
        given-names: T. A.
      - family-names: Proper
        given-names: H. A.
